'''Melanie Smith''' {{born|16|December|1962}} is a former actress who played [[Tora Ziyal]] in {{s|DS9}}. She was the third, final, and most frequent actress to play the role. 

Smith has also had recurring roles on {{wt|Seinfeld}} (1994, with [[Jason Alexander]]), {{wt|Melrose Place}}, ''The Division'', and {{wt|As the World Turns}}. She starred with [[Andrew Robinson]] and [[Stephen Macht]] in {{wt|Trancers III}} (1992, starring [[Tim Thomerson]]) and has also had single guest-starring appearances in {{wt|Curb Your Enthusiasm}}, {{wt|The Adventures of Brisco County, Jr.}}, and {{wt|Nowhere Man (American TV series)|Nowhere Man}} (1996, starring [[Bruce Greenwood]]).

Following her acting career, she became a life coach and in 2023 authored the self-help book ''Unfinished Business.'' In 2025 she released a jazz album ''The Broken and the Breaker.''

