'''John Durbin''' is the Iowa-born actor who played the role of [[Ssestar]] in the {{s|TNG}} [[TNG Season 1|first season]] episode {{e|Lonely Among Us}}. He went on to appear again on ''The Next Generation'', playing [[Gul]] [[Lemec]] in the [[TNG Season 6|sixth season]] episode {{e|Chain Of Command, Part I}} and {{e|Chain Of Command, Part II}}. He later appeared as [[Traidy]] in the {{s|DS9}} [[DS9 Season 5|fifth season]] episode {{e|A Simple Investigation}} and as [[Telsian miner 003|Telsian Miner]] in the {{s|VOY}} [[VOY Season 7|seventh season]] episode {{e|Critical Care}}. His costume from his very first ''Star Trek'' appearance in {{e|Lonely Among Us}} was sold off on the [[It's A Wrap! sale and auction]] on eBay. {{stala|9510}}

Durbin made his acting debut as a corpse in {{wt|The Return of the Living Dead}} (1985, featuring [[Drew Deighan]] and makeup by [[Ken Myers]]). Durbin would go on to have similarly small roles in films such as {{wt|Tapeheads}} (1988, with [[Lee Arenberg]], [[Katy Boyer]], [[Mary Crosby]] and [[John Fleck]]), {{wt|Dead Man Walking (film)|Dead Man Walking}} (1988, with [[Jeffrey Combs]], [[Leland Crooke]] and [[Biff Yeager]]), ''Cyborg 2'' (1993, with [[Tracey Walter]]), {{wt|Heart and Souls}} (1993, starring [[Alfre Woodard]], with [[David Paymer]], [[Wren T. Brown]], [[Janet MacLachlan]] and [[Kurtwood Smith]]), and {{wt|Kansas City (film)|Kansas City}} (1996). He also appeared in {{wt|Mr. Jones (1993 film)|Mr. Jones}} (1993, with [[Lauren Tom]], [[Thomas Kopache]], [[Irene Tsu]], [[Scott Thomson]] and fellow ''Deep Space Nine'' guest [[Albert Henderson]]).

Durbin has, however, occasionally been seen in larger supporting roles. Such was the case in films like ''The Blue Iguana'' (1986, co-starring [[Dean Stockwell]]), {{wt|Dr. Caligari (film)|Dr. Caligari}} (1989, featuring [[Marjean Holden]]), {{wt|Checking Out (1989 film)|Checking Out}} (1989, with [[Ian Wolfe]] and [[Ann Magnuson]]), {{wt|King of the Hill (1993 film)|King of the Hill}} (1993), and {{wt|Ride with the Devil (film)|Ride with the Devil}} (1999, with [[Zach Grenier]]). He was later seen in ''Take Out'' (2005, with [[Daniel Roebuck]]).

Outside of his ''Star Trek'' appearances, Durbin's guest starring credits include {{wt|The A-Team}} (starring [[Dwight Schultz]], with [[Lance LeGault]]), {{wt|Hunter (1984 American TV series)|Hunter}} (1986, starring [[Charles Hallahan]], with [[Brent Spiner]] and series regular [[Bruce Davison]]), {{wt|Crime Story (American TV series)|Crime Story}} (1987, starring [[Bill Smitrovich]], with [[Armin Shimerman]]), {{wt|Max Headroom (TV series)|Max Headroom}} (starring [[Matt Frewer]], with [[W. Morgan Sheppard]] and [[Concetta Tomei]]), {{wt|Melrose Place}}, {{wt|Providence (American TV series)|Providence}} (with Concetta Tomei), and {{wt|Angel (1999 TV series)|Angel}} (with [[Daniel Dae Kim]], [[John Rubinstein]] and [[Keith Szarabajka]]). Durbin was seen in such made-for-TV movies as ''Tricks of the Trade'' (1987, with Armin Shimerman), {{wt|Dead Solid Perfect}} (1988, with [[Bibi Besch]] and [[Brett Cullen]]), {{wt|O Pioneers! (film)|O Prioneers!}} (1992, with [[Deborah May]]), {{wt|The Burden of Proof (miniseries)|The Burden of Proof}} (1992, with [[Adrienne Barbeau]], [[Neal McDonough]], [[Gail Strickland]] and Concetta Tomei), {{wt|And the Band Played On (film)|And the Band Played On}} (1993, with [[Christopher Carroll]], [[Reg E. Cathey]], [[David Clennon]], [[Ronald Guttman]], Thomas Kopache, [[Dakin Matthews]], [[Lawrence Monoson]], [[Jeffrey Nordling]], [[Saul Rubinek]]), and {{wt|Truman (1995 film)|Truman}} (1995, with [[Holmes R. Osborne]] and [[Harris Yulin]]). He was also part of the cast of {{wt|The Shining (miniseries)|The Shining}} (1997, starring [[Steven Weber]]).

