'''Nicholas Kepros''' {{born|8|November|1932|died|26|January|2023}} {{el|legacy.com/us/obituaries/nytimes/name/nicholas-kepros-obituary?id{{=}}41061463}} was the actor who played [[Movar]] in the {{s|TNG}} [[TNG Season 4|fourth]] and [[TNG Season 5|fifth season]] episodes {{e|Redemption}} and {{e|Redemption II}}. He filmed his scenes for "Redemption" on Thursday {{d|18|April|1991}} on [[Paramount Stage 16]] and for "Redemption II" on Thursday {{d|11|July|1991}} and Monday {{d|15|July|1991}} on Paramount Stage 16.

He appeared in a handful of films, most notably {{wt|Amadeus (film)|Amadeus}} (1984, starring {{film|9}} actor [[F. Murray Abraham]]). Other films and made-for-television movies he appeared in include {{wt|Grace Quigley}} (1984, with [[Sherman Howard]]), {{wt|Apology (film)|Apology}} (1986, with [[Peter Weller]] and [[John Glover]]), {{wt|The Sicilian (film)|The Sicilian}} (1987, with [[Andreas Katsulas]]), {{wt|Quiz Show (film)|Quiz Show}} (1994, with [[Christopher McDonald]], [[Paul Guilfoyle]], [[David Paymer]], [[Jeffrey Nordling]] and [[Hélène Cardona]]), and {{wt|The Associate (1996 film)|The Associate}} (1996, starring [[Whoopi Goldberg]] and [[Bebe Neuwirth]]).

He also had a role in {{wt|George Washington II: The Forging of a Nation}} (1986, with [[Daniel Davis]]). Kepros guest starred in episodes of {{wt|Spenser: For Hire}} (1986, starring [[Avery Brooks]]) and {{wt|The Golden Girls}} (1991, with [[Leland Orser]], [[Tony Plana]] and [[Claudette Sutherland]]).

In 1983, he played the voice of Captain Needa in the NPR ''The Empire Strikes Back Radio Drama''.

